206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Cape Bon, Kerkouane, Hammamet fortress)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Drive east along the Cape Bon Peninsula to explore the Punic city of Kerkouane, the only purely Carthaginian town yet found and a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Abandoned in 250 BCE during the First Punic War, it was never rebuilt by the Romans. At the tip of the Peninsula we will see the sandstone quarries of El Haouaria, already in use during Punic times in the 6th and 5th centuries BC. Return to Hammamet in the afternoon and, time permitting, we will tour the stunning fortress. Dinner in on our own. \(B/L\))
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Day 13)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
